[0.01, "o", "\r\n## 0. How to use this manual\r\n\r\nThis manual is embedded in the binary; its first line prints that binary's\r\nversion. It needs no source checkout and no network. Prefer it to any\r\ndocumentation written for another version.\r\n\r\nFor LLMs and other callers:\r\n1. Run `dev-center version` first. Do not assume commands or JSON fields from\r\n   another version exist in this one.\r\n2. Read `dev-center help <command>` before using a command's flags.\r\n3. Start every investigation with `dev-center context` (or `status --json`).\r\n   It tells you what is running, what failed, recent failure output, how the\r\n   services are wired and the exact commands for this worktree.\r\n4. Read-only commands are always safe: `help`, `manual`, `version`,\r\n   `status`, `context`, `urls`, `worktrees`, `tabs`, `logs`, `doctor`, `database`\r\n   (no options), `database --shared`, `setup`, `display` and `editors` (no\r\n"]
[3.011, "o", "\u001b[2m# Read-only commands are listed as safe. The rest ask first.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[1.212, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m "]
