[0.013, "o", "   options), `main` (fetches, changes nothing), `create --dry-run`,\r\n   `open --dry-run`.\r\n5. These change the developer's machine; use them when the developer asked\r\n   for that, otherwise ask first:\r\n   - what runs: `start`, `stop`, `restart`, `run`, `send`, `gui`\r\n   - navigation only: `tabs select N` (does not start or stop services)\r\n   - worktrees and data: `create`, `delete --confirm`, `database --sql`,\r\n     `--shared-dump` (can download hundreds of MB), `--empty`,\r\n     `database --reset --confirm`, `main --update`\r\n   - settings: `setup`, `display`, `editors` with options; `open`; `update`\r\n"]
